# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  LPAD — Logos Privacy-Preserving Token Launchpad .gitignore
#  A fresh clone + `bash setup.sh` should produce a buildable tree
#  with no per-machine state. Anything generated, downloaded, or
#  user-specific stays out.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# External LEZ source, symlinked in by setup.sh
_lez

# Claude Code session settings (per-machine tool-permission allowlist) + the
# project's review/agent tooling.
.claude/
**/.claude/

# Devin skills (OpenSpec workflow tools). Another agent's tooling, like .claude/
# above: not lpad source, and nothing a clone needs to build, test or deploy.
.devin/
.devinignore

# ── Internal design docs + RFP sources + grant proposal ────────────
# Kept local; not part of the published code repo. The committed CLI reference
# lives at cli/README.md instead. Drop these lines if you want docs in-repo.
# `docs/*` rather than `docs/`: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so a negation below could not re-include anything.
docs/*
# The privacy document is the one exception, and it is not a preference: both
# RFPs require it by name as a deliverable - "Provide a privacy and anonymisation
# properties document covering: what on-chain state and transaction data is
# visible to observers; what data is protected when the private account path is
# used; trust assumptions ...; and what happens if a user bypasses the expected
# interaction path" (requirements1.md:359, requirements2.md:330). Ignoring it
# would leave that requirement with no artefact behind it in the public repo.
!docs/PRIVACY.md
requirements1.md
requirements2.md
proposal.md

# ── Rust / Cargo build artefacts ───────────────────────────────────
target/
**/target/
*.rlib
*.rmeta
Cargo.lock.bak

# ── Nix build artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
result
result-*
.direnv/
.envrc.cache

# ── Mini-app build outputs (regenerated by nix build) ──────────────
mini-app/dist/*.lgx
mini-app/core/lib/*.so
mini-app/core/lib/*.so.*
mini-app/**/result
mini-app/**/result-*

# ── Bootstrap / runtime state ──────────────────────────────────────
scripts/*.env
*.log
/tmp-*

# ── Editor / OS cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Local `cargo vendor` output, used only to build guests without network egress.
/vendor/

# Bootstrap OUTPUT: generated per-run, contains live ids. Not source.
/scripts/bootstrap*.env
